rmath of hunting.”\n- Frames 24–25 show the bird being placed into a storage compartment on the snowmobile.\n- Frames 26–30 show the adult inspecting the snowmobile’s controls while the child watches.\n\n→ This sequence supports the idea that the snowmobile situation occurs *after* the hunting activity.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion on Answer “4: Their snowmobile can't reverse”**\n\n→ **The answer is NOT correct based on visual evidence.**\n\nWhile the snowmobile is stationary and the adult is inspecting its controls (possibly the gear shifter), there is **no definitive visual proof** that the snowmobile *cannot reverse*. There is no sign of it being stuck, blocked, or mechanically broken. The adult’s actions suggest curiosity or routine adjustment, not troubleshooting a reverse gear failure. No distress or active problem-solving related to inability to reverse is shown.\n\nThe snowmobile may simply be parked while the family handles the hunted bird and prepares for departure — a normal pause, not a malfunction.\n\n---\n\n✅ **Final Verdict: Answer '4' is incorrect.** There is insufficient visual evidence to support the claim that the snowmobile cannot reverse."}, {'batch_start': 180, 'batch_end': 210, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1615.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1616.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1617.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1618.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1619.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1620.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1621.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1622.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1623.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1624.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/