owmobile is parked on flat, open snow with no visible obstructions behind it. There is no visual cue that it is stuck, blocked, or mechanically impaired. The man’s actions (storing gear, talking to camera) suggest normal operation.\n\n**6. Do people show signs of distress or problem-solving related to the snowmobile?**  \n→ **No.** The man’s expressions (frames 16–24) show him talking, possibly narrating or reacting to the hunt — he is not showing distress, frustration, or attempting to fix anything. His actions are calm and procedural (storing the bird).\n\n---\n\n**Temporal Sequence Analysis:**\n\n- Frames 1–15: Depict the aftermath of a hunt — the boy holding the bird, walking back, and handing it to the man.\n- Frames 16–24: The man is standing next to the snowmobile, talking to the camera — likely narrating the experience.\n- Frames 25–30: The man opens the snowmobile’s storage compartment and places the bird inside — a routine post-hunt action.\n\nThere is **no transition** from hunting to a snowmobile malfunction. The snowmobile is simply being used for storage and transport — not experiencing any reverse gear issue or mobility problem.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe claim that “their snowmobile can’t reverse” is **not supported by any visual evidence** in these frames. The snowmobile is stationary, but for logistical reasons (storing the hunted bird), not due to mechanical failure. There is no indication of reverse gear issues, distress, or attempts to move the vehicle backward.\n\n✅ **Answer '4' is incorrect.**"}, {'batch_start': 120, 'batch_end': 150, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1555.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1556.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1557.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1558.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1559.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data