itioned in a way that suggests it cannot move backwards (e.g., stuck, blocked, or mechanical issue)?**  \n→ **No.** The snowmobile is parked on open snow, with no visible obstruction behind it. There is no indication of it being stuck in snow, blocked by an object, or suffering a mechanical failure. The position is neutral and typical for parking.\n\n---\n\n**6. Do people show signs of distress or problem-solving related to the snowmobile?**  \n→ **No.** The man (vlogger) is smiling and laughing in Frame 23–24 while shaking hands with another man. The boy is walking happily toward the snowmobile. There are no signs of distress, frustration, or attempts to fix or move the snowmobile manually.\n\n---\n\n**Temporal Sequence from Hunting Aftermath to Snowmobile Situation:**\n\nThe frames do not show any hunting activity or its aftermath. The sequence begins with the man standing near a snowmobile (Frame 1), then transitions to him driving a truck (Frames 8–18), then exiting the truck (Frames 19–20), entering a building (Frame 21), and interacting with people and a snowmobile outside (Frames 22–24). There is **no visual or contextual link to “second hunting”** in these frames, nor any indication that the snowmobile’s inability to reverse is a consequence of hunting.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThere is **no evidence in the 30 frames** to support the claim that “Their snowmobile can't reverse.” The snowmobile is simply parked, and the family appears to be in a relaxed, social setting — possibly preparing for or returning from an activity, but not dealing with any mechanical issue.\n\n✅ **Therefore, answer ‘4’ is incorrect based on the visual evidence provided.**"}, {'batch_start': 360, 'batch_end': 371, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1795.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1796.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KbahC-QCKU8/frames/frame_1797.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/video